
plan2040 on cpu_rp2040
  ls            list /dev and bin/
  help          builtins, grammar, often needed (reboot, bootsel, ...)
running built-in 'boot' automatically...
% date
date: not found (try 'ls')
% toggle /dev/buttons/lamp /dev/lamp &
[1]
% help
grammar:  stage [| stage ...] [< path] [> path | >> path] [&]   # comment
          stage := program [arg...]      quotes: "..." or '...'

write a file:  cat > <path>   (replace)    cat >> <path>   (add to end)
               type lines, end with '.' or Ctrl-D

internal commands (shell builtins, not in ls; output can't be piped):
  help                 this text
  jobs                 list background jobs
  kill %<id>           stop a background job
  sleep <ms>           pause the shell, everything else keeps running
  run <name>           replay a script (/fram/<name>, else built-in)
  loop <name>          replay a script forever, Ctrl-C to stop
  scripts              list built-in scripts (files: ls /fram)
  watch <ms> <stage..> repeat a pipeline every <ms>, Ctrl-C to stop
everything else is a program or a file, pipes ok: ls, ls -l /fram

often needed:
  echo bootsel > /dev/reboot           USB bootloader: copy a new .uf2 now
  echo now > /dev/reboot               plain reboot
  echo YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS > /dev/rtc  set the clock (date shows it)
  mkfs /fram                           format: files gone, hours kept
  df, ls -l /fram, cp, mv, rm          space, files, copy, rename, remove
  cat /dev/hours                       power-on hours (set: /dev/hours/ctl)
  cat > /fram/crontab                  timed jobs (on/off: /dev/cron)
  hexdump [-s off] [-n len] <path>     raw bytes, e.g. /dev/fram, /dev/mem
% exit 0
